==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|biðja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*bidjaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|bitten}}, {{cog|fo|biðja}}, {{cog|da|bede}}, {{cog|sv|bedja}}, English [[bid]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈpɪðja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪðja|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bað|báðu|beðið}}

# to [[ask]], to [[request]] {{+obj|is|acc<someone> + gen<for something or some action><q:optionally>}}
#: {{syn|is|beiðast}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''bað''' þig nú bara um [[greiði|greiða]].|I just '''asked''' you a [[favor]].}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[pray]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''bið''' til [[Guð]]s.|I '''pray''' to [[God]].}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s5|b|i|ð|j=j}}

